WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
DEAD RECKONING: BLACKOUT
A playable Mars mission: predict what will keep six crew safe.

00:03.000 --> 00:07.000
A finite budget. A real choice.
Store spare energy in a battery, align solar arrays, or save the Parts.

00:07.000 --> 00:11.000
Earth is quiet. Your colony keeps working.
Radio delay and dust affect different systems. Compressed training time.

00:11.000 --> 00:15.000
Your first result is preserved.
Actual mission reserves show what the battery preparation changed.

00:15.000 --> 00:21.000
One mission. Two futures.
Replay the same colony and events with solar alignment. Compare the evidence.

00:21.000 --> 00:25.000
NASA evidence. Clear model limits.
Historical records inform the mission; the game labels its simplified rules.

00:25.000 --> 00:28.960
Predict. Observe. Compare. Explain.
An anonymous learning record turns play into a science discussion.
